NAME
    gfx - userspace framebuffer test card (Path C demo)

SYNOPSIS
    gfx [SECONDS]

DESCRIPTION
    Maps the VBE framebuffer into the calling process's address space,
    paints a test card (color bars, RGB gradient, centered rect, full-
    width cross), holds for SECONDS (default 4), then releases the
    framebuffer so fbcon can resume.

    Only one task may own the framebuffer at a time. While owned,
    fbcon mutes its text painting; on release, the next fbcon write
    repaints the console.

    The pixel format depends on the VBE mode the bootloader negotiated.
    On the default QEMU setup that's 1024x768 at 24bpp (BBGGRR per
    pixel triple). `sys_fb_info` returns the actual width/height/pitch/
    bpp so portable code can pack pixels correctly.

SYSCALLS USED (session 107)
    SYS_FB_INFO   (72)   read framebuffer geometry
    SYS_FB_MAP    (74)   map FB at chosen user VA + take ownership
    SYS_FB_UNMAP  (88)   release ownership (auto on task exit)

EXIT STATUS
    0   FB was painted and released
    1   FB unavailable (boot lacked VBE) or another task owns it

NOTES
    The framebuffer is mapped at user VA 0x50000000 by this demo.
    For a 1024x768x24 mode that's 2.25 MiB (≈576 pages).
